diff --git a/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/README.md b/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c1c0b78
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+> **The listfile is a WXL module**: `wxl_listfile.dll`, built from this folder, loaded from `WXL\Modules\` by the
+> 64-bit client. It sees the client only through `Engine/Source/WXL/Sdk/wxl_api.h`; its public interface for other
+> modules is `Engine/Source/WXL/Sdk/wxl_listfile_api.h`.
+> Test: `Tools/WxlModuleTest/listfile_host_test.cpp` (the module through the C ABI, `run_listfile_tests.sh` runs it all).
+
+# Listfile: file id -> file path
+
+Turns a file id into a path using `<client folder>\WXL\listfile.csv`. When the file is not found it hands back a
+**"not found" name** that the client cannot open, so the client's own handling takes over: its default green texture
+for a `.blp`, its default checkered cube for an `.m2`. Everything that is looked for and not found goes to the log.
+
+## The listfile
+
+```
+1;interface/cinematics/logo_800.avi
+53183;sound/music/citymusic/darnassus/darnassus intro.mp3
+```
+
+One entry per line: `<id>;<path>`. Read as the community listfiles write it:
+
+* the delimiter is `;` or `,`; CRLF or LF; spaces in paths are kept; `/` is turned into `\` when the path is handed out
+* a header row is optional: if the first non-blank line does not start with a number it is skipped
+* a UTF-8 BOM is skipped; ids go up to 4294967295
+* the same id twice: **the first entry wins**; a line that is not `<id>;<path>` is skipped and counted in the log
+
+## Switching it on: `WXLExtendedEquipment.ini`
+
+```ini
+[Listfile]
+Eager=1                          ; 1 = build the lookup table at load (default); 0 = read the file at run time
+Path=WXL\listfile.csv            ; relative to the client folder, or absolute
+CheckExists=1                    ; 1 = also ask the client whether the file the listfile names is really there
+NotFoundName=WXL\NotFound        ; the name handed out for a file that is not found (.blp / .m2 is added by kind)
+```
+
+| | `Eager=1` (default) | `Eager=0` |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| At load | reads the whole file into memory | reads nothing |
+| A lookup | a binary search, ~0.5 µs | streams the file until the id is found (first lookup of an id near the end of a 185 MB file: ~0.07 s), then the answer is cached, hits and misses both |
+| Memory | about the size of the file on disk (3,000,000 lines, 185 MB: ~150 MB held, ~350 MB at the peak of the build, 1 s) | a cache of up to 65,536 answers |
+| An edit to the file | seen after `reload()` | seen after `reload()` (the cache is dropped) |
+
+Neither mode needs the file to exist at load: without it the module still loads, logs that it cannot open it, and
+answers "not found" for every id.
+
+## Not found
+
+A file counts as not found when its id is not in the listfile, or (with `CheckExists=1`) when the listfile names it but
+the client cannot open it. The answer is `WXL_LISTFILE_NOTFOUND` and `out` holds the not-found name:
+
+| The caller says it is | `out` | The client then |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| a texture (`WXL_LISTFILE_TEXTURE`, or a path ending `.blp`) | `WXL\NotFound.blp` | cannot open it: uses its own default (green) texture |
+| a model (`WXL_LISTFILE_MODEL`, or `.m2` / `.mdx`) | `WXL\NotFound.m2` | cannot open it: uses its own default (checkered cube) model |
+| anything else (`.mp3`, `.avi`, ...) | `WXL\NotFound` | cannot open it |
+
+The kind only picks the extension, so the engine sends the name down the loader that has the right fallback. The base
+name is `[Listfile] NotFoundName`; pick one that is not a real file in any archive. Nothing is generated and the module
+serves no files of its own.
+
+Log category `LISTFILE`, one line per missing thing, once (not once per lookup):
+
+```
+file id 4000001 is not in the listfile (texture): answering 'WXL\NotFound.blp'
+file id 2 -> 'interface\cinematics\wow_intro_800.avi' is not in the client (any type): answering 'WXL\NotFound'
+'sound\music\nothing.mp3' is not in the client (any type): answering 'WXL\NotFound'
+```
+
+Note this is what the *lookup functions* answer. Nothing here intercepts the client's own file opens: a texture the client
+asks for by itself, without going through this module, behaves as it always did.
+
+## Using it from another module
+
+```cpp
+#include "wxl_listfile_api.h"
+
+const WxlListfileServices* lf = WxlListfileGet(api);          // NULL when the listfile module is not loaded
+char path[260];
+switch (lf->resolve(fileId, WXL_LISTFILE_TEXTURE, path, sizeof(path)))
+{
+    case WXL_LISTFILE_FOUND:    /* path is the file's own path */                          break;
+    case WXL_LISTFILE_NOTFOUND: /* path is the not-found name: open it anyway and the
+                                   client shows its own missing texture / model */         break;
+    default:                    /* WXL_LISTFILE_ERROR: bad arguments or buffer too small */ break;
+}
+```
+
+| Function | |
+| --- | --- |
+| `lookupPath(id, out, size)` | the listfile's path for an id, nothing else: no existence check, no not-found name |
+| `resolve(id, kind, out, size)` | the path to open for an id: its own, or the not-found name for `kind` |
+| `resolvePath(path, kind, out, size)` | the same for a path you already have (`kind` `WXL_LISTFILE_ANY` = by extension) |
+| `entryCount()`, `isEager()` | the table's size (0 at run time), and the mode |
+| `reload()` | read the listfile again |
+
+Modules load in file-name order: a module that wants the service *while it initializes* must sort after
+`wxl_listfile.dll` (name it `20_mymodule.dll`), or fetch it on first use. Every function is thread-safe.
diff --git a/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/Resolver.cpp b/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/Resolver.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8d3428f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/Resolver.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@
+// See Resolver.hpp.
+// Copyright (C) 2026 WarcraftXL (GPLv3, see Engine/Source/WXL/Event.h)
+
+#include "Resolver.hpp"
+
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstring>
+
+namespace wxl::listfile
+{
+    namespace
+    {
+        constexpr size_t kMaxLoggedKeys = 20000;   // distinct missing files logged before the log stops growing
+
+        std::string Backslashes(const char* path)
+        {
+            std::string s(path);
+            for (char& c : s) if (c == '/') c = '\\';
+            return s;
+        }
+
+        bool EndsWith(const std::string& s, const char* ext)
+        {
+            const size_t n = std::strlen(ext);
+            if (s.size() < n) return false;
+            for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i)
+            {
+                char c = s[s.size() - n + i];
+                if (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z') c = static_cast<char>(c - 'A' + 'a');
+                if (c != ext[i]) return false;
+            }
+            return true;
+        }
+
+        uint32_t KindOfExtension(const std::string& path)
+        {
+            if (EndsWith(path, ".blp")) return WXL_LISTFILE_TEXTURE;
+            if (EndsWith(path, ".m2") || EndsWith(path, ".mdx")) return WXL_LISTFILE_MODEL;
+            return WXL_LISTFILE_ANY;
+        }
+
+        const char* KindName(uint32_t kind)
+        {
+            return kind == WXL_LISTFILE_TEXTURE ? "texture" : kind == WXL_LISTFILE_MODEL ? "model" : "any type";
+        }
+    }
+
+    void Resolver::Configure(Table* table, Hooks hooks, bool checkExists, std::string notFoundName)
+    {
+        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m_lock);
+        m_table = table;
+        m_hooks = hooks;
+        m_checkExists = checkExists;
+        m_notFoundName = Backslashes(notFoundName.c_str());
+        m_logged.clear();
+        m_logFull = false;
+    }
+
+    void Resolver::LogMissing(const std::string& key, const char* what)
+    {
+        {
+            std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m_lock);
+            if (m_logged.size() >= kMaxLoggedKeys)
+            {
+                if (m_logFull) return;
+                m_logFull = true;
+                if (m_hooks.log) m_hooks.log("not-found log is full: further distinct missing files are not logged");
+                return;
+            }
+            if (!m_logged.insert(key).second) return;   // this one was reported already
+        }
+        if (m_hooks.log) m_hooks.log(what);
+    }
+
+    // The name the client gets for a file that is not found. It is not a file anywhere: opening it fails, and the
+    // client's own handling for a texture (the green one) or a model (the cube) takes over. The extension is there
+    // so the engine sends it down the right loader.
+    std::string Resolver::NotFoundFor(uint32_t kind) const
+    {
+        if (kind == WXL_LISTFILE_TEXTURE) return m_notFoundName + ".blp";
+        if (kind == WXL_LISTFILE_MODEL)   return m_notFoundName + ".m2";
+        return m_notFoundName;
+    }
+
+    int Resolver::Deliver(const std::string& path, int result, char* out, size_t outSize)
+    {
+        if (!out || path.size() + 1 > outSize) return WXL_LISTFILE_ERROR;
+        std::memcpy(out, path.c_str(), path.size() + 1);
+        return result;
+    }
+
+    int Resolver::LookupPath(uint32_t fileId, char* out, size_t outSize)
+    {
+        if (!m_table || !out || outSize == 0) return -1;
+        std::string path;
+        if (!m_table->Lookup(fileId, path))
+        {
+            char msg[160];
+            std::snprintf(msg, sizeof(msg), "file id %u is not in the listfile", fileId);
+            LogMissing("id:" + std::to_string(fileId), msg);
+            return 0;
+        }
+        return Deliver(path, 1, out, outSize) == WXL_LISTFILE_ERROR ? -1 : 1;
+    }
+
+    int Resolver::ResolvePath(const char* rawPath, uint32_t kind, char* out, size_t outSize)
+    {
+        return ResolveImpl(rawPath, kind, out, outSize, nullptr);
+    }
+
+    // fileId, when the path came from a lookup, goes into the log line so one missing file is one line.
+    int Resolver::ResolveImpl(const char* rawPath, uint32_t kind, char* out, size_t outSize, const uint32_t* fileId)
+    {
+        if (!rawPath || !*rawPath || !out || outSize == 0) return WXL_LISTFILE_ERROR;
+        const std::string path = Backslashes(rawPath);
+
+        const bool there = !m_checkExists || !m_hooks.exists || m_hooks.exists(path.c_str());
+        if (there) return Deliver(path, WXL_LISTFILE_FOUND, out, outSize);
+
+        if (kind == WXL_LISTFILE_ANY) kind = KindOfExtension(path);
+        const std::string answer = NotFoundFor(kind);
+        std::string msg = fileId ? "file id " + std::to_string(*fileId) + " -> '" + path + "'" : "'" + path + "'";
+        msg += " is not in the client (" + std::string(KindName(kind)) + "): answering '" + answer + "'";
+        LogMissing("path:" + path, msg.c_str());
+        return Deliver(answer, WXL_LISTFILE_NOTFOUND, out, outSize);
+    }
+
+    int Resolver::Resolve(uint32_t fileId, uint32_t kind, char* out, size_t outSize)
+    {
+        if (!m_table || !out || outSize == 0) return WXL_LISTFILE_ERROR;
+
+        std::string path;
+        if (m_table->Lookup(fileId, path))
+            return ResolveImpl(path.c_str(), kind, out, outSize, &fileId);   // in the listfile: is it in the client?
+
+        // Not in the listfile: nothing is known about it but what the caller expects it to be.
+        const std::string answer = NotFoundFor(kind);
+        char msg[320];
+        std::snprintf(msg, sizeof(msg), "file id %u is not in the listfile (%s): answering '%s'", fileId, KindName(kind), answer.c_str());
+        LogMissing("id:" + std::to_string(fileId), msg);
+        return Deliver(answer, WXL_LISTFILE_NOTFOUND, out, outSize);
+    }
+}
diff --git a/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/Resolver.hpp b/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/Resolver.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e07aa6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Engine/Source/WXLModules/Listfile/Resolver.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+// The module's public behaviour: look an id up, and hand out a not-found name when the file is not there.
+// Copyright (C) 2026 WarcraftXL (GPLv3, see Engine/Source/WXL/Event.h)
+//
+// Engine-free: what it needs from the client (does this file exist? write a log line) comes in as two functions,
+// so the tests drive it without one.
+#pragma once
+
+#include "ListfileTable.hpp"
+
+#include "wxl_listfile_api.h"
+
+#include <mutex>
+#include <string>
+#include <unordered_set>
+
+namespace wxl::listfile
+{
+    struct Hooks
+    {
+        bool (*exists)(const char* clientPath) = nullptr;   ///< can the client open it? null = assume yes
+        void (*log)(const char* line) = nullptr;
+    };
+
+    class Resolver
+    {
+    public:
+        /// @param notFoundName the base of the name handed out for a file that is not found, e.g. "WXL\\NotFound"
+        ///        (.blp / .m2 is appended by kind). It must not be a file the client has.
+        void Configure(Table* table, Hooks hooks, bool checkExists, std::string notFoundName);
+
+        int LookupPath(uint32_t fileId, char* out, size_t outSize);
+        int Resolve(uint32_t fileId, uint32_t kind, char* out, size_t outSize);
+        int ResolvePath(const char* path, uint32_t kind, char* out, size_t outSize);
+
+    private:
+        int ResolveImpl(const char* path, uint32_t kind, char* out, size_t outSize, const uint32_t* fileId);
+        std::string NotFoundFor(uint32_t kind) const;
+        int Deliver(const std::string& path, int result, char* out, size_t outSize);
+        void LogMissing(const std::string& key, const char* what);   // once per key
+
+        Table*      m_table = nullptr;
+        Hooks       m_hooks;
+        bool        m_checkExists = true;
+        std::string m_notFoundName;
+
+        std::mutex  m_lock;
+        std::unordered_set<std::string> m_logged;
+        bool        m_logFull = false;
+    };
+}
